# Both docker-compose.yml and docker-compose.gpu.yml already bind-mount the
# WHOLE ./fastocr/weight host directory over /app/fastocr/weight at runtime
# (read-only) -- that mount replaces the image's copy of the directory
# entirely regardless of what COPY put there, so baking FastOcr.pth into the
# image only wastes build time/image size (and duplicates a large binary
# across every image layer/registry push) without ever actually being used.
# Excluding it here also makes the mount NON-optional: a container started
# without that volume (e.g. a bare `docker run`) will fail fast on missing
# weights instead of silently falling back to whatever was baked in at
# build time.
fastocr/weight/FastOcr.pth
